# Always deploy the site after portal changes

Whenever you finish changes that players see on the web portal (anything under `docs/`, `functions/`, `worker/`, `migrations/`, `tools/generate_site.py`, `wrangler.toml`, `wrangler.worker.toml`), **deploy and verify** before ending the turn.

## Steps

1. Regenerate HTML if copy/layout changed: `python tools/generate_site.py`
2. Commit only portal-related files (ask first if commit policy is unclear; if the user said «заливай» / deploy, commit + push is implied).
3. Push `main` → GitHub Action **Deploy Worker** (`.github/workflows/deploy-worker.yml`) runs `wrangler deploy -c wrangler.worker.toml`. Requires repo secret `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (one-time: `python tools/set_github_cf_secret.py` with a real `.cf_token`).
4. Smoke-check live host: `https://aquatech.santcrail.workers.dev/`
   - home loads, header/auth shell works
   - `/api/catalog` returns 200
   - login/register pages show player copy (no pages.dev / D1 / workers.dev marketing jargon)
   - Action already runs `smoke_portal_and_versions.py` with `STRICT_LIVE_DEPLOY=1` after deploy
5. Prefer workers.dev for player links; `*.pages.dev` may be blocked on some networks.

Local fallback if CI secret is missing: `python tools/deploy_to_cloudflare.py worker`

## Copy

Strip AI-slop from player-facing text (anti-ai-slop-writing skill). Keep store/case descriptions short and concrete.
